oultry]] \n\n==Ingredients==\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 2 cups cooked [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] or [[Cookbook:Turkey|turkey]]\n* 1 small can (8–10 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounce]]) [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushrooms]], drained\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n* 3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Broth|clear chicken broth]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Peanut|peanuts]]\n* Cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Melt butter in [[Cookbook:Wok|wok]] or [[Cookbook:Skillet|skillet]].\n# [[Cookbook:Stir-frying|Stir-fry]] celery and onions.\n# Add chicken and mushrooms and stir over lowered heat 5 minutes.\n# Combine (in separate bowl) cornstarch, soy sauce, and broth; slowly add to hot mixture in wok and cook 5 minutes.\n# Stir in peanuts.\n# Serve over hot rice.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* You could use [[Cookbook:Cashew|cashews]].\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Midwestern U.S. recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mushroom|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using peanut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Gluten-free recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Stir fry recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Peanut Chicken Stir-Fry","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 tablespoons butter","sourceText":"2 tablespoons butter","amountText":"2 tablespoons butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¾ cup celery","sourceText":"¾ cup celery","amountText":"¾ cup celery","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null